  "id": "unet_classifier",
  "name": "U-Net classifier (Fashion-MNIST)",
  "description": "Classification with a U-Net: the encoder, decoder and skip connections of the U-Net example, then AdaptiveAvgPool2d, Flatten and Linear give 10 class scores. Fashion-MNIST's 28\u00d728 images are resized to 32\u00d732 so that three halvings fit (32 \u2192 16 \u2192 8 \u2192 4), and the filters are halved (16/32/64, bottleneck 128) so that it trains on a CPU server. For this task a plain CNN such as the Small CNN example is smaller and faster; this one shows how a segmentation network becomes a classifier.",
